  "notes": "The priest's Communion under the species of bread, kept in one document because it is one act: the verse said as he genuflects and rises, the threefold Dómine non sum dignus said striking his breast, and the form said as he signs himself with the Host. The three repetitions are encoded as three sets of words with their own ids, as the Kyrie is; the rubric telling the priest to go on secretly is printed inside each of the three lines and is carried three times, because that is where the change of voice falls. ACCÍPIAM at w003 is future indicative, not present subjunctive, the two being identical in form: it is coordinated with invocábo, which can only be future. TANTUM at w018 is the adverb, not the neuter of tantus. SUB at w014 governs the accusative here, motion under a roof, where the corpus's other token of the word (ordinarium.credo w080) governs the ablative.",
